{"shortDescription":"The Canadian dollar weakened to around 1.39 per USD following the release of domestic and US employment data.Employment in Canada declined by 41,700 in August, missing expectations for a 15,000 increase and following a 75,100 gain in July.The weak labor data could support a more dovish stance from…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Canadian dollar weakened to around 1.39 per USD following the release of domestic and US employment data."]},{"type":"p","children":["Employment in Canada declined by 41,700 in August, missing expectations for a 15,000 increase and following a 75,100 gain in July."]},{"type":"p","children":["The weak labor data could support a more dovish stance from the BoC. Meanwhile, US payrolls increased by 162,000, about three times the consensus estimate."]},{"type":"p","children":["The strong report boosted expectations for a September Fed rate hike."]},{"type":"p","children":["This backdrop could widen the interest-rate differential between the US and Canada, favoring the US dollar over the loonie."]},{"type":"p","children":["The BoC kept its key policy rate unchanged at 2.25% at its September meeting, as widely expected."]},{"type":"p","children":["However, it noted that inflation risks had increased, while new tariffs had made the growth outlook more uncertain."]},{"type":"p","children":["The BoC left the future path of monetary policy open, saying it would adjust policy as needed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Governor Macklem said policymakers were prepared to raise rates if inflation remained elevated."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:581316:0","title":"Canadian Dollar Weakens on Jobs Data","published":1788527503,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/canada/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"F